---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE, LEGAL_OPERATOR } from "../data/legal";
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Service — NovaGuard"
  description="The rules, responsibilities and service conditions that apply when NovaGuard is added to or used in a Discord server."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-12 sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
    <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.25em] text-ink-muted uppercase">
      Effective {LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE}
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-display mt-4 text-3xl sm:text-5xl">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
      These terms govern access to the hosted NovaGuard Discord bot, dashboard and website
      operated by {LEGAL_OPERATOR.name} in the {LEGAL_OPERATOR.country}. By adding NovaGuard to a
      server, configuring it or using its commands, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree,
      do not use the service.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-12 border-t border-line pt-7">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl">1. Eligibility</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        You must meet{" "}
        <a
          href="https://discord.com/terms"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
          class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 hover:text-primary"
        >Discord's minimum age</a>
        for your country and any higher minimum required by applicable law. If you are not legally
        able to accept these terms yourself, a parent or legal guardian must accept them for you.
        You must use a valid Discord account and may not evade Discord restrictions, suspensions
        or age requirements.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 border-t border-line pt-7">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl">2. What NovaGuard provides</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        NovaGuard provides optional community tools such as moderation, logging, setup,
        configuration, levels, economy, voice statistics, tickets, giveaways, reminders,
        GitHub updates, status information and AI-assisted answers. Features depend on Discord,
        hosting and third-party providers and may differ between servers. No feature is promised
        to remain available permanently.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 border-t border-line pt-7">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl">3. Server administrator responsibilities</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 space-y-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        <p>
          A server owner or administrator decides whether NovaGuard is installed, which optional
          features are enabled, which roles can use them and where logs or results are posted. They
          are responsible for having authority to make those choices and for complying with the
          rules and laws that apply to their community.
        </p>
        <p>
          Administrators must explain relevant uses to members before enabling optional message
          logging, behavioral features or AI, use proportionate settings, keep a human moderation
          and appeal route, restrict log channels, and never use NovaGuard to infer sensitive
          traits, conduct unlawful surveillance or make legally significant automated decisions.
          Organizations that require a data-processing agreement must contact the operator before
          using NovaGuard for processing that requires one; these terms alone are not such an
          agreement. NovaGuard provides a practical{" "}
          <a href="/server-admin-notice" class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 hover:text-primary">Server Admin Notice</a>
          that administrators can adapt and share with their members.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 border-t border-line pt-7">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl">4. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">You may not use or attempt to use NovaGuard to:</p>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted marker:text-primary">
        <li>break applicable law, Discord's Terms, Developer Policy or Community Guidelines;</li>
        <li>harass, threaten, discriminate against, exploit or invade the privacy of another person;</li>
        <li>spam, manipulate engagement, scrape data or build profiles across communities;</li>
        <li>upload malware, attack, probe, overload, reverse engineer or bypass service controls;</li>
        <li>obtain credentials, tokens, private exports or data you are not authorized to access;</li>
        <li>train an AI model on Discord data obtained through NovaGuard;</li>
        <li>misrepresent NovaGuard output as guaranteed, professional or human-reviewed advice.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 border-t border-line pt-7">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl">5. Content, commands and AI output</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 space-y-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        <p>
          You retain any rights you hold in content submitted through Discord. You grant only the
          limited permission needed to receive, process and return that content for the command or
          feature you request. Do not submit secrets, credentials or content you have no right to
          process.
        </p>
        <p>
          AI and automated output can be incomplete, inaccurate or inappropriate. Verify important
          information independently. NovaGuard is not a substitute for legal, medical, financial,
          safety or other professional advice, and AI output must not be the sole basis for a
          decision that materially affects another person.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 border-t border-line pt-7">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl">6. Privacy and third-party services</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        The <a
          href="/privacy"
          class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 hover:text-primary"
        >Privacy Policy</a> explains NovaGuard's processing, retention, providers, cookies and
        individual controls. NovaGuard depends on services including Discord, Cloudflare, Oracle,
        Google Drive, GitHub and, when enabled, Anthropic. Their own terms and policies also apply
        to their services. You must not use NovaGuard in a way that causes the operator to violate
        those provider rules.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 border-t border-line pt-7">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl">7. Security</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        Keep Discord accounts, server permissions and exported files secure. Report suspected
        vulnerabilities or unauthorized access privately to{" "}
        <a
          href={`mailto:${LEGAL_OPERATOR.privacyEmail}`}
          class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 hover:text-primary"
        >{LEGAL_OPERATOR.privacyEmail}</a> and allow a reasonable period to investigate before any
        public disclosure. Never include active tokens, passwords or another person's private data
        in a public report.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 border-t border-line pt-7">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl">8. Availability and changes to the service</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        NovaGuard is provided on an “as available” basis. Maintenance, provider failures, rate
        limits, security incidents or development changes may interrupt or alter the service. The
        operator may add, change, limit or retire features and may impose reasonable safeguards or
        usage limits. Where practical, material planned changes will be announced through the
        website or configured Discord update channels.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 border-t border-line pt-7">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl">9. Suspension and termination</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        Access may be limited or terminated where reasonably necessary for security, provider
        compliance, legal obligations, abuse prevention or a material breach of these terms.
        Administrators may stop using NovaGuard by removing it from their server. Members may stop
        using commands and can use the export and erasure controls described in the Privacy Policy.
        Provisions that logically survive termination, including security, disclaimers, liability
        and governing law, remain effective.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 border-t border-line pt-7">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl">10. Disclaimer and liability</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 space-y-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        <p>
          To the extent permitted by law, NovaGuard is provided without warranties of uninterrupted
          availability, fitness for a particular purpose, error-free operation or preservation of
          every community record. Administrators remain responsible for moderation decisions,
          permissions, notices and independent recovery plans appropriate to their community.
        </p>
        <p>
          To the extent permitted by law, the operator is not liable for indirect, incidental,
          special or consequential loss arising from use or unavailability of NovaGuard, including
          loss caused by third-party services or administrator configuration. Nothing in these
          terms excludes liability, remedies or mandatory consumer rights that applicable law does
          not allow to be excluded or limited.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 border-t border-line pt-7">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl">11. Governing law and disputes</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Moldova, without removing any
        mandatory protection you have under the law of your residence. Before filing a dispute,
        contact the operator and allow a reasonable opportunity to resolve it informally. Disputes
        not resolved informally may be brought before a competent court. Privacy complaints may
        also be made to the authority identified in the Privacy Policy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 border-t border-line pt-7">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl">12. Changes and contact</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        Material changes will be published here with a new effective date and an additional notice
        where required. Continued use after a change takes effect constitutes acceptance only to
        the extent permitted by law. Questions about these terms can be sent to{" "}
        <a
          href={`mailto:${LEGAL_OPERATOR.contactAddress}`}
          class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 hover:text-primary"
        >{LEGAL_OPERATOR.contactAddress}</a>{" "}
        at any time. The operator is {LEGAL_OPERATOR.name}, contactable by
        email in the {LEGAL_OPERATOR.country}.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
